# Standalone Base 9B smoke test: CPython 3.12, Windows/Linux x86-64, CUDA 12.8.
# Separate from requirements.txt (AI Toolkit / ordinary training).
# Compile with uv 0.10.9; requirements-smoke.txt pins transitive dependencies too.
# Metadata resolution and source API inspection are NOT CUDA execution validation.
# Use requirements-smoke.txt in a fresh CPython 3.12 environment, not this input
# file and not together with the broad ordinary-training requirements.txt.
# The +cu128 pins select CUDA wheels explicitly; a compatible NVIDIA driver is
# still required. CPU test execution uses the existing environment, not this lock.
# bitsandbytes is included for the optional AdamW8bit choice. PEFT, TensorBoard,
# and wandb are not needed for the default standalone smoke command; do not enable
# optional logging flags with this specification.
#
# Verified without installation (uv 0.10.9): 64-package universal resolution, then
# binary-only resolution of the resulting lock for CPython 3.12 on both
# x86_64-pc-windows-msvc and x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu. No package builds or Python
# downloads were allowed. The local Python is 3.14, so this is metadata/wheel
# verification, not execution of the pinned Python 3.12 environment.
# Exact versions include transitive dependencies, but this is not an artifact
# hash lock. Other platforms/Python versions have not been verified.
#
# API references inspected:
# https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers/blob/v0.37.0/src/diffusers/pipelines/flux2/pipeline_flux2_klein.py
#   Flux2KleinPipeline, Qwen3 prompt helper, latent/text ID helpers.
# https://github.com/huggingface/accelerate/blob/v1.12.0/src/accelerate/accelerator.py
#   prepare/backward/clip/unwrap, step-skipped property, cleanup methods.
# https://github.com/bitsandbytes-foundation/bitsandbytes/blob/0.49.2/bitsandbytes/optim/optimizer.py
#   AdamW8bit state1/state2 and step counter (CUDA behavior still unverified).
# https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/v4.51.3/src/transformers/models/qwen3/modeling_qwen3.py
#   Qwen3 is present at the corrected broad minimum; smoke pins 5.3.0 below.
# https://pytorch.org/get-started/previous-versions/
#   Official Torch 2.10.0 / Torchvision 0.25.0 CUDA 12.8 pairing.
--index-url https://pypi.org/simple
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128
torch==2.10.0+cu128
torchvision==0.25.0+cu128
diffusers==0.37.0
transformers==5.3.0
accelerate==1.12.0
bitsandbytes==0.49.2
safetensors==0.7.0
pillow==12.1.1
tqdm==4.67.3
